                <pb facs="0313" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jordan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-10T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                                1921—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 12—1:20
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>76. My 74, November 3, 11 a.m.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d208-f1"/> Memorandum in
                    reply received today from Haitian Government containing following points: <list>
                        <label>1st.</label>
                        <item>Haitian Government considered that protocol of October 3rd,
                                1919,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d208-f2"/> has lapsed and that a loan
                            cannot now be contracted under this instrument which no longer
                            exists.</item>
                        <label>2d.</label>
                        <item>That it is impossible to consent to having all the revenues of the
                            Republic pledged for 30 years for the payment of a loan of
                            $14,000,000.</item>
                        <label>3d.</label>
                        <item>That even if it be granted that the protocol of October 3rd, 1919,
                            still exists the Haitian Government persists in believing that the
                            conditions thereof being modified by the amount of the new loan it is
                            not [<hi rendition="#italic">now</hi>] necessary that the terms of a new
                            protocol be studied.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Translation of memorandum by mail.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d208-f3"/></p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jordan</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
